    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d733">

                <pb facs="0761" n="753" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg753"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/447: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Taylor</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-06T17:00:00-04:00">July 6, 1938—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Canadian Government in a note dated June 28,<anchor n="19" xml:id="d733-f1"/>
                    copy of which is being sent to you by mail, expresses some doubt as to
                    feasibility of setting up continuing body “at a time when the League of Nations
                    is endeavoring to coordinate and centralize existing refugee organizations and
                    to break down the differentiations between the various classes or groups of
                    refugees.” Canadian Government also states that points (2) and (3) of agenda
                    raise difficult problems under Canadian immigration laws.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
